id: scouter
name: Scouter
kind: gear
itemType: accessory
tags: tech
craftDC: Variable (Qualified ~ Grandmaster)
# Which, asked when it is given: it is the Concealment Check it asks for.
craftDCChoices: qualified, expert, master, grandmaster
# "Tier of Power 2+ (Qualified) or 3+ (Expert)" - the Tier a Power Up destroys it at.
breaksAt: qualified=2, expert=3
# "During a Combat Encounter, you can spend 1 Action to attempt to scan the strength of
# another Character. Characters may attempt a Concealment Skill Check equal to the Craft DC."
placeCost: 1
scanSkill: concealment
scanCombatOnly: true
# Hidden from it for the rest of the Encounter, whatever their Holding Back does.
scanHoldingBack: false
source: Core Rule
description: >
  An Action in combat to read someone's Tier of Power - and their Power Level, if they are at
  their base Tier - unless they hide it with a Concealment Check at its Craft DC. Also a
  Communicator.
text: >
  Scouter [Tech]: A more advanced, wearable version of the Scout Scope, this one functions as
  a Communicator as well.
  –Craft DC: Variable (Qualified ~ Grandmaster)
  –Effects: During a Combat Encounter, you can spend 1 Action to attempt to scan the strength
  of another Character. Characters may attempt a Concealment Skill Check equal to the Craft DC
  of this Scouter to try and avoid being scanned. If they succeed, nothing happens and they
  automatically succeed on any further Concealment Skill Checks to avoid being spotted by a
  Scouter for the remainder of the Combat Encounter. If their current Tier of Power is the
  same as their base Tier of Power, you also learn of their Power Level.

  If the Craft DC of a Scouter is Expert or lower, it can be destroyed when a Character of
  Tier of Power 2+ (Qualified) or 3+ (Expert) uses the Power Up Maneuver within 15 Squares of
  you, or when within several hundred miles while Adventuring.

  While you have this Accessory equipped, you have access to the Scan Adventuring Maneuver.
  The Scouter also functions as a Communicator.

---

# --- What the system does ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Given: its Craft DC, Qualified to Grandmaster, which is the Concealment Check it asks for.
#
# Scan, while worn and during a Combat Encounter: 1 Action at the one targeted, and the same
# card the Scout Scope's has. Read tells the scanner their current Tier of Power, and their
# Power Level when that is their base Tier. Hidden lasts the rest of the Encounter against
# every Scouter, with no Holding Back clause - the entry has none.
#
# Qualified or Expert, its row says Fragile, and every Power Up at Tier 2+ (3+ for Expert)
# names it on its card: which were within 15 Squares is the table's, and so is throwing
# it away.
#
# --- What is not built ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The Scan Adventuring Maneuver, and being destroyed while Adventuring: there are no
# Adventuring rules in this system yet. Communicator: said at the table, as the
# Communicator's own entry is.
